Test case 1:
Optimize impedance matching using single stub matching by finding the location and length of the stub for the values of load impedance of to 350200 keeping the characteristic impedance Zo= 60 Q constant .

AIM: To optimize impedance matching using single stub matching by finding the location and length of the stub for the values of load impedance of 100 300 to 3$0_ 300 keeÅjug the characteristic impedance Zo= 60 Q constant.

CODE:
clc;
clear;
close;
Zo = 60;
f = 100*(10^6);
// Wavelength
lo = 3*(10^8)/f;
// Phase constant
beta = 2*%pi/lo;
// Load impedance values
ZR_values = 100:50:350;
printf("Load Impedance\tK\t\tS1 (m)\t\tStub Length (m)\n");
printf("-------------------------------------------------------------\n");
for i = 1:length(ZR_values)
ZR = ZR_values(i);
// Reflection coefficient
K = (ZR-Zo)/(ZR+Zo);
// Magnitude of K
ampK = abs(K);
// Phase angle
phi = atan(imag(K)/real(K));
if real(K) < 0 then
phi = phi + %pi;
end
// Point of stub attachment (Given formula)
S1 = (phi+%pi-acos(ampK))/(2beta);
// Length of stub (Given formula)
L = (lo/(2%pi))atan(sqrt(1-ampK^2)/(2ampK));
printf("%f\t%f\t%f\t%f\n",ZR,ampK,S1,L);
end

